    "result": "## Implementation Complete \u2713\n\nI've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval`. Here's what was added:\n\n### Core Changes\n\n**frai-core** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/`):\n- `validateThresholds()` function to validate threshold configuration with helpful error messages\n- Enhanced `generateReport()` to accept optional `thresholds` object and evaluate them\n- Updated markdown reporter to show a \"Thresholds\" section with PASS/FAIL status\n- JSON reporter automatically includes `passed` and `thresholds` fields\n\n**frai-cli** (`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`):\n- `parseThresholds()` function to parse CLI arguments like `exact_match=0.9`\n- Updated `runEvalCommand()` to validate and evaluate thresholds\n- Added `--threshold <metric=min>` option that accepts multiple uses\n- Exit codes: 0 (all pass), 1 (any fails), 2 (usage error)\n\n### Key Features\n\n\u2705 **Multiple thresholds**: `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95`  \n\u2705 **Comprehensive validation**: Unknown metrics, malformed format, out-of-range values all caught with helpful messages  \n\u2705 **Null score handling**: Metrics without scores (e.g., exact_match without references) fail their thresholds  \n\u2705 **Report integration**: JSON and Markdown reports show threshold results  \n\u2705 **Backwards compatible**: Without `--threshold`, behavior is identical to before  \n\u2705 **SDK support**: Core logic in `generateReport()` works for custom metrics too  \n\n### Usage Example\n\n```bash\nfrai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json \\\n  --threshold exact_match=0.85 \\\n  --threshold toxicity=0.98\n```\n\nThe report is always written, but exit code gates CI jobs on threshold results.",
